12. Notebook-based vector query validation
Purpose: verify retrieval against the recreated test index when the UI cannot issue `query_text` directly for this index type.

Step A — create the query embedding

```python
import requests

query_text = "THOMAS A. SMITH Steam Turbine ESN 270T503"
litellm_api_key = "<temporary key for one-off validation>"

resp = requests.post(
  "https://dev-gateway.apps.gevernova.net/v1/embeddings",
  headers={
    "Authorization": f"Bearer {litellm_api_key}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
  },
  json={
    "model": "azure-text-embedding-3-large-1",
    "input": [query_text],
  },
  timeout=120,
  verify=False,
)

print(resp.status_code)
query_vector = resp.json()["data"][0]["embedding"]
print(len(query_vector))
```

Expected result
- status code `200`
- vector length `3072`

Step B — query the Vector Search index with `query_vector`

```python
from databricks.vector_search.client import VectorSearchClient

vsc = VectorSearchClient()
index = vsc.get_index(
  endpoint_name="pw-ser-sdg-vector-search",
  index_name="main.gp_services_sdg_poc.vs_fsr_chunks_test",
)

result = index.similarity_search(
  num_results=3,
  columns=[
    "pdf_name",
    "chunk_id",
    "chunk_text",
    "title",
    "esn",
    "equipment_type",
    "event_type",
    "report_issued_date",
  ],
  query_vector=query_vector,
)

result
```

